{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":42,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T01:58:58.867807395Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"7387ed3c-671c-45b9-9c6b-7de095f1dc16","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"Plan: Add a focused unit test to packages/core/test/session-run-coordinator.test.ts that verifies the interrupt fence kills a RUNNING TOOL (a child fiber spawned inside the drain), not just the drain wrapper. This is the cheapest discriminating test for the #510 placebo concern (does interrupt truly kill a running fiber vs. a 204 no-op?). The handler session.interrupt -> SessionExecution.interrupt -> coordinator.interrupt -> Fiber.interrupt(entry.owner); testing coordinator.interrupt directly exercises the exact fence the handler triggers. Two cases: (1) interrupt propagates to a forkChild tool fiber (its exit is an interruption, owner interrupted, active cleared); (2) no orphan — after interrupt the key is free and a fresh run starts (tool child not leaked). Will run bun test to verify, then gated commit.","created_at":"2026-08-29T01:58:58.861452912Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAyGnLmfhWhwFN5CyiJqSJiFea2Pld9tsf36Uavp7gCZCFySZTA7t5+L96/vV130erwgPKt+86kqqIQE9Jd+btAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNLQq/tMaymsy2MoYeky88w60kiKIus2oRBiOdzz/utHfeAkO13hyk5SOfF0rPd0X/CUwae6utDOZXvdxB+SxAA="}
