{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":45,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T02:07:04.007436877Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"c8e033bc-c69e-48bf-a279-98b6990a0b94","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"Result: Added handler-unit-test coverage for the SessionRunCoordinator interrupt fence (issue #510, branch feature/stop-button, commit 78a02a8b).\n\nWHAT: Two new tests in packages/core/test/session-run-coordinator.test.ts exercise the exact fence the stop-button handler triggers — session.interrupt -> SessionExecution.interrupt -> coordinator.interrupt -> Fiber.interrupt(entry.owner):\n1) 'kills a running tool child fiber when interrupted' — a tool running as a forkChild of the drain is interrupted (exit is an interruption), the owner fiber is interrupted, and active is cleared. This is the #510 placebo test: it proves interrupt truly kills a running fiber rather than returning a 204 no-op that leaves the tool alive.\n2) 'does not leave the tool child running after interrupt (no orphan)' — after interrupt kills the tool, the key is free so a fresh run starts (no leaked tool holding the session). This mirrors the #510 'no orphan after UI restart' point at the fence level.\n\nWHY: The prior live 6-point probe could not observe a running generation/tool fiber (agent on that server spawns no shell-tool children; generations finish <2s), so the core #510 concern — does interrupt actually kill a running fiber? — was UNVERIFIED (placebo risk). A unit test at the fence is the cheapest discriminating test and is deterministic.\n\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based. 18/18 coordinator tests pass; core 'bun typecheck' clean. Regression-guard validated by temporarily replacing Fiber.interrupt(entry.owner) with Effect.void — both new tests then time out/fail as expected — then reverted.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: The full server handler round-trip (HttpApi session.interrupt -> SessionExecution) is not exercised here; it is a thin delegation (handlers/session.ts:368 -> SessionExecution.interrupt -> coordinator.interrupt), already proven by code-inspection in prior phases. The test targets the fence itself, which is where the placebo risk lives. No integration/cassette run was needed.","created_at":"2026-08-29T02:07:03.999991656Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAeJTb4Q+4rQ+STAj74DPdhrTk1V3HgkDgSxNhYr4u9oSVcUa9aBL2rBfIhU8nwB6BMYoTqr/N2zdUH2pKBbkyAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA/o8/FSPR+1ITTfG33bTxPgQfAZ/J99bcUOLwl9SQC37KjOvfjVncRgexIQSgFUV9WAo7GP0guh7LcWOyAHKgo="}
