rship (Fiber+active), §12 Resource (LLM stream / tool Process / retry Deferred lifetimes & settlement signals incl. pgrep 0), §13 External Boundary (SDK→handler→coordinator thin delegation, 204 vs settle, unavailability 404 no-op).\n- Instantiate docs/conformance/Stop-Button-Conformance-Suite.md (430 lines) covering all 36 universal dimensions, grounding §§14-16 in live probe 7-9 + coordinator concurrent tests and the debounce-orphan fix; §§24/30 adversarial review marked BLOCKED pending fresh context.\n\nWHY: Placebo 204 while fiber/tool/401-429 lives is worse than no button, and a debounce orphan that silently blocks retry after cancel is a temporal correctness violation (§15) that hides behind model-permitted transitions. Mechanical enforcement (statechart owns lifecycle, engine schedules via Fiber.interrupt) requires both the pure gate and the temporal/transport discriminating tests.\n\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based. tui 235 pass 1 skip 613→1183 expects (46 files), core 1107 pass 0 fail, core typecheck clean, probe bash -n OK and probe_exit 3 SKIP (server down) rehearsed, machine file zero-imports arity-2 pure verified. Regression guard: prior placebo tests still pass (Fiber.interrupt neuter would fail).\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: tui tsgo --noEmit SIGTERM/OOM in this env (tui core typecheck clean via tsc + bun test instead); handler round-trip integration thin delegation only code-inspected; live tool-child still N/A on :49374 (covered at coordinator seam); adversarial review §§24/30 still BLOCKED (requires fresh zero-context); Phase5 hardening (Kani/proptest + @xstate/test execution) deferred. Commit f19df87c on feature/stop-button.","created_at":"2026-08-29T17:31:15.472717379Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAMv9BDwfUdjkvKGDjwAVFKjo3ouTDDV/Zx8F1r