{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":106,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T17:31:44.603764462Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"bcf180bb-c197-43d6-90b8-56d1203931cd","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"Result: Pure machine transition and forbidden tests — state and transition conformance per Universal Checklist §§5-8 delivered and verified on feature/stop-button commit f19df87c (#510).\n\nWHAT: Two-primitive bounded machine (idle/running/confirming/interrupting, 11 events, 16 permitted, 28 forbidden) per Verified Spec §4.3 is now exhaustively exercised:\n\n- §5 State Model Completeness — 10 audits: states/events/guards/permitted/forbidden/effects/identity/ownership/settlement/invariants/concurrency/external boundaries — each with explicit isPermitted/nextState evidence; timing stays in shell (arity 2 purity).\n- §6 State Conformance — per-state correspondence, entry/exit, guards, effects, no-bypass (idle cannot reach interrupting, confirming cannot reach idle directly), invalid/unknown handling (unknown event → undefined/false), abstractions documented.\n- §7 Transition Conformance — 16 permitted transitions each verified for event implemented, source-state enforced, guard enforced (isPermitted), destination reached (nextState), required effects (dialog/fence/no-op/settle), unauthorized effects absent, identity/ownership preserved, ordering preserved (primary path + ESC bypass), discriminating verification per transition, traceability to spec §4.3/§7 edges.\n- §8 Forbidden Transitions — 28 forbidden as complement of 4×11−16; barrier is absence from ReadonlyMap; defined behaviour (false/undefined); discriminating test (isPermitted↔nextDefined invariant over all 44 pairs); plausible mutation detection (forbidden count 28, permitted 16, spot-check idle SETTLED/confirming STOP_CLICK remain forbidden); prior gap fixed (running ESC/INTERRUPT_API now present as forbidden, 26→28).\n\nWHY: Without exhaustive forbidden coverage a spurious transition (e.g. idle YES→confirming) would be a silent state-corruption placebo; the 28-entry audit makes the gate checkable without mocking I/O (AGENTS.md cheapest-test-first).\n\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based. fork tui 44 pass 723 expects (stop-button-machine.test.ts), tui full 236 pass 1 skip 1183 expects, core 1107 pass (plus 24 identity/ownership/resource tests 67 expects), tsc --noEmit passes, probe-stop-button-phase0.sh bash -n OK and 9-point (concurrency 7, temporal 8, transport 9) SKIPs when server down, PASS when live. Machine file has zero imports, STOP_BUTTON_EVENTS/TRANSITIONS/forbiddenTransitions exports for audit.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: Live 9-point probe points 2/3/5/6 remain N/A on no-tool-child server (tool sleep 42 not spawned) — covered at coordinator seam by existing Fiber+active tests; full fork bun test --workspace not re-run; interactive TUI debounce-orphan manual QA (Stop→No→Stop within 1s) relies on try/finally + YES-path gate now verified via unit timer.\n\nCommitted at f19df87c (debounce orphan fix + 9-point probe + conformance suite §§5-16 per Universal Checklist) — no new commit needed this session; working tree clean for stop-button sources.\n\nNext: Phase1c adversarial review of Verified Spec + conformance suite (§9) before hardening.\n","created_at":"2026-08-29T17:31:44.596507246Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA+kejxiPnR3ywZh6gr8n4h0cBhA4AdUYLYZGnABk1sH6dTt5/o+bdM3lbbQtXKxxC3pxwHObA/a20xqq+he1PAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAA