{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":115,"timestamp":"2026-08-30T19:56:51.865082409Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"d62b025f-010d-41c9-b688-57fcac8b32a8","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=plan posted; test suites re-run (tui 235/1183, core 1107/3043, machine 44/723 all match claims); machine+index.tsx wiring inspected next=finish spec↔code vocabulary + conformance dimension audit, then post review verdict blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:56:51.858925212Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAj4vWB2jDhmEw9LwCEei6Y9xAgxZcX4+JKT9+kBVAJlYLJfqE3DLNlwkr9EX416kzb4BiCnrmipYoGxjPC/90Bw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEunBb+RUFY40sY9xNLk+w7AK4ju2TJZXGTY3bK/VtsEbJ6kv04x0rKs5m9MJxcCfB7KdhdEvwY6Mnc9LUTDagY="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":116,"timestamp":"2026-08-30T19:58:06.079538641Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"43d21e56-3e9e-41da-a98c-305abd03bebe","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"[REVIEW] state=verifying completed=review of stop-button state machine + verification architecture vs Verified Spec §4/§5/§7 + Universal Checklist. 6 findings (2 model/spec contradictions, 1 architectural, 3 doc). Delegating safe fixes to Builder.\n\nFINDING F1 (HIGH, model↔spec contradiction): Machine forbids running:ESC, but Verified Spec §7 E11 requires running+ESC(single)→stay running. The test stop-button-machine.test.ts:86 *enshrines* running:ESC as forbidden — it is wrong vs the spec it claims to conform to. The TUI handles single-Esc by incrementing a counter outside the machine, so the machine cannot validate E11. FIX: add running:ESC→running to TRANSITIONS (pure self-transition); update test + conformance §5 counts (16→17 permitted, 28→27 forbidden).\n\nFINDING F2 (HIGH, architectural — headline): The machine is consulted only as a *static validation gate* (isPermitted/nextState), never as the system of record. deriveStopState() reconstructs state from 3 independent shell booleans (isRunning,isInterrupting,isConfirming) with a hardcoded priority order (interrupting>confirming>running>idle) that is itself an un-modeled guard. SETTLED is never dispatched into the machine; the machine's interrupting→idle edge is dead. Authoritative idle is the SSE status (time.idle), not the machine. This inverts Verified Spec §3b.2 ('statechart owns lifecycle, engine only schedules') and the conformance §5 claim that SETTLED 'maps to TUI 800ms cooldown as observed projection'. DECISION NEEDED: (a) make the machine the system of record (hold a state signal; dispatch PROMPT_SUBMIT/STOP_CLICK/YES/NO/DONE/ERROR/SETTLED from real sources incl. SSE settlement) OR (b) downgrade §3b.2 to 'machine is a validation gate; SSE is authoritative for lifecycle'. Recommend (a) for the 'no placebo' guarantee (I2) to be enforceable by the machine.\n\nFINDING F3 (MED, missing path): running:INTERRUPT_API (external concurrent interrupt from another client/API) is unmodeled — forbidden in machine and the TUI never subscribes to a server-pushed interrupt, so an external interrupt is silently invisible. Spec §7 has no running:INTERRUPT_API edge (E13 only covers interrupting:INTERRUPT_API). The authoritative POST /api/session/:id/interrupt is the whole point of the feature; a concurrent external one must also reach interrupting. FLAG: add running:INTERRUPT_API→interrupting to spec + machine + TUI subscription (not applied; spec gap).\n\nFINDING F4 (MED, UX/placebo-adjacent): confirming+DONE/ERROR race (drain completes while dialog open) — spec deliberately forbids confirming→idle, so the dialog lingers showing 'Stop agent?' after the agent already stopped; clicking Yes logs 'interrupt success' + toasts 'Interrupted' on a no-op (placebo-misleading, exactly the Failure-Matrix risk the feature exists to prevent). FIX (cheap, applied): capture wasRunning at interrupt issue; on 204 against an already-idle session, toast 'No active run' + log 'interrupt no-op (already idle)' instead of 'Interrupted'/'interrupt success'. Keep spec's no-auto-dismiss design.\n\nFINDING F5 (LOW, doc drift): Verified Spec §1.3/§3b.3 call the probe a '6-point probe'; the shipped scripts/probe-stop-button-phase0.sh has 9 points (concurrency/temporal/transport added, commit '9-point live probe'). Conformance §5 correctly says 9. FIX (applied): update spec wording 6→9.\n\nFINDING F6 (LOW, abstraction gap): (a) Spec §6.1 locates the machine at session-ui/src/v2/components/prompt-input/machine.ts but it is colocated as stop-button-machine.ts in prompt/ — acceptable but not per spec. (b) Spec §3b.2 says transitions emit a declarative effect descriptor (invokeInterrupt|openDialog|toast) the shell interprets; the machine only returns nextState — the shell re-derives effects via deriveStopState+routing, not via a machine-emitted descriptor. (c) confirming:YES guard !isInterrupting (spec §4.3) is correctly omitted from the *pure* machine (timing stays in shell per §3b.2 purity) but the spec table lists it as a machine guard — doc inconsistency, not a bug. (d) I6 raced wake/run (WAKE/RUN events) is not modelable in the machine (only PROMPT_SUBMIT exists); lives in coordinator only — consistent with purity boundary, note it.","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:58:06.072529760Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAY0wC9E+gXjAzjL23TBP7hjWccfOUINfqumgRfkyBSu9YvWe34PwrnR0t2xfqqd7TAMMTlmlKGKkdmPFwSRu4BQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOaGcxED9YGhSxbiYiWOsun2+Bgb0GbAszZOy2o0KwVD9LvoKE/t7DysW0ecWqnZWgU8PCasg77GXioC7h0NHAY="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":117,"timestamp":"2026-08-30T19:58:16.365543679Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"9e970df4-c58e-4a6e-84ab-1fe317dfca48","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"[result] REVIEW — stop-button evidence & traceability per expanded brief (#510, feature/stop-button @ f19df87c). Reviewer role (read-only); findings reported, no code edits.\n\n== VERIFIED (claims match re-executed evidence) ==\n- Test pass-counts re-run, not trusted: tui 235 pass / 1 skip / 1183 expects (claim 235/1183 ✓); core 1107 pass / 3043 expects (claim 1107 ✓); stop-button-machine 44 pass / 723 expects (claim 44/723 ✓); core targeted 42 pass / 97 expects ✓.\n- Machine structure matches spec edge catalog: 4 states, 11 events, 16 permitted transitions, 28 forbidden (4×11−16) ✓.\n- Debounce-orphan fix present in index.tsx: try/finally resets isConfirming (L369); lastInterruptAt 1s debounce gate at the YES→interrupting fence only (L389-396); 800ms isInterrupting cooldown in finally (L413) ✓.\n- ESC_ESC path gated via machine: isPermitted(cur2,'ESC_ESC') + stopNextState (L568-574) ✓.\n- No stubs/TODO in stop-button code (the single TODO@540 is pre-existing, unrelated); probe bash -n OK ✓.\n- BLOCKED scope honestly marked: §24 Adversarial, §30 Reviewer Gate BLOCKED; live tool-child points 2/3/5/6 N/A on no-tool-child server (covered at coordinator seam); handler integration code-inspected only; Phase5 Kani/proptest deferred. No false PASS.\n\n== TRACEABILITY DRIFT (documentation only — no code defect) ==\n- A1 (Med): Conformance suite cites machine test = '12 tests 153 expects' (§28/§34/§60/§111/§361) but actual = 44 tests / 723 expects; coordinator '18 tests' also stale (now 20). The conformance record it claims to be is self-inconsistent.\n- A2 (Med): Verified Spec §4.3 permitted-transition TABLE lists 14 r